\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Proposition}
\title{Positive mass gives an invertible response}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Let #{L} be the \vocabk{weighted graph Laplacian}{fdip-0007}
on a finite vertex set #{V}, with positive real edge weights, and
let #{m>0}. Its \vocabk{massive precision}{fdip-000A}
#{Q_m=m^2I-L} is a \vocabk{positive precision parameter}{fdip-0004}
and an \vocabk{isomorphism}{ca-0015}. Its \vocabk{Green operator}{fdip-000A}
#{G_m=Q_m^{-1}} is \vocabk{self-adjoint}{fdip-001P} and strictly positive.
For each source field #{j}, the unique solution of #{Q_mf=j} is
##{f=G_mj,\qquad f(v)=\sum_wG_m(v,w)j(w).}
For every vertex #{w}, its \vocabk{Green kernel}{fdip-000A} column
is the unique field satisfying
##{Q_mG_m(\cdot,w)=\delta_w.}
These assertions include disconnected graphs. On the empty vertex
set the unique endomorphism is an isomorphism, and there are no
point-source columns.}
\proof{
\p{The Laplacian is self-adjoint, and adding the scalar identity
preserves self-adjointness. The energy identity in \ref{fdip-0008}
gives, for #{f\ne0},
##{\begin{aligned}
\langle f,Q_mf\rangle_V
 &=\langle f,(-L)f\rangle_V+m^2\sum_v f(v)^2\\
 &=\sum_e w(e)(\extd_{\mathbb R}f)(e)^2\\
 &\quad+m^2\sum_v f(v)^2>0.
\end{aligned}}
Thus #{Q_mf=0} implies #{f=0}. Finite dimension and rank-nullity
make this injective endomorphism surjective, so it is an isomorphism.
The inverse-response lemma \ref{fdip-001Q} gives a self-adjoint
inverse and the unique solution #{f=G_mj}. For #{j\ne0}, write
#{x=G_mj\ne0}; then
##{\langle j,G_mj\rangle_V=\langle Q_mx,x\rangle_V>0.}
On the empty vertex set the same map argument gives the unique
isomorphism of zero modules.}
\p{The kernel column at #{w} is #{G_m\delta_w}. Multiplying by
#{Q_m} gives the point-source equation, and inverse response gives
uniqueness. The counting indicator expansion
#{j=\sum_wj(w)\delta_w} and linearity give the displayed response
sum after evaluation at #{v}. No vertex-volume factor occurs because
the vertex pairing and indicators are counting. On an empty carrier
this expansion is the empty sum.}
}
\p{The argument combines the incidence energy in \ref{fdip-0008}
with inverse response in \ref{fdip-001Q}. The lattice precision
comparison in the \vocabk{massive Green construction}{fdip-000A} uses
\citet{Section 4, Equations (4.2)-(4.5), p. 3}{wingate2025lattice}
and \citet{Theorem 8.26, p. 399}{friedli2017statistical}; their
lattice and boundary conventions remain part of that comparison.}
